/* Glasspole — the Windows resource block.
 *
 * ICON ID 1, AND THE NUMBER MATTERS. Explorer, the taskbar and the Alt-Tab
 * switcher all show an executable's icon with the LOWEST numeric ID, not the
 * first one declared. Anything else here would have to stay above this.
 *
 * The path is relative to this file, and the icon lives at the repository root
 * because tadpole.exe and tadpole-view.exe embed the same one — one logo, one
 * file, three executables. Regenerate it from glasspole.png with
 * tools/make-icon.py; it is committed so that a Windows build needs no image
 * library.
 *
 * Compiled only on Windows: CMakeLists.txt adds this to the target inside
 * if(WIN32), because windres does not exist in a Linux build and a .rc means
 * nothing to ELF. */
1 ICON "../../glasspole.ico"
